offset  size  field
0       4     total_len = 384
4       8     magic = ASCII FGANRS01
12      2     version = 1
14      2     header_len = 384
16      2     result: 1 ACCEPTED, 2 REJECTED
18      2     error: 0 NONE, 1 INVALID, 2 UNAVAILABLE, 3 CONFLICT, 4 INTERNAL
20      8     request_id
28      8     producer_epoch
36      16    run_id
52      16    consumer_id
68      2     mapping_name_ascii_len, 1..128 when accepted; zero when rejected
70      2     reserved_zero
72      128   mapping_name_ascii, zero-padded; accepted prefix is
               `Local\\ForgeAnalysisRing-`
200     4     slot_count; zero when rejected
204     4     slot_payload_capacity_bytes; zero when rejected
208     8     slot_stride_bytes; zero when rejected
216     8     total_mapping_bytes; zero when rejected
224     32    forge_protocol_hash
256     32    forge_analysis_ring_schema_hash
288     32    SHA-256 of the exact 256-byte request
320     32    worker_build_hash
352     4     flags: bit0 LIVE_MAPPING; bit1 OBSERVER_ONLY; other bits zero
356     24    reserved_zero
380     4     CRC32C over bytes [0,380)

Idempotence and lifecycle
-------------------------

An exact retry of `(producer_epoch, request_id)` returns the same response and
mapping identity. Reuse with different request bytes is CONFLICT. Registration
is accepted only before Run Prepare, and the mapping is never resumed after a
worker or daemon restart. Every restart uses a fresh producer_epoch. The daemon
publishes a SampleBlock to this disposable branch only after the canonical
record has been admitted to the journal. Ring full drops the newest analysis
copy, latches the branch fault, and never blocks acquisition or journal seal.
